.TH CVEC_POP 3 "2026-07-10" "c_collections" "C Collections Library - Macros"
.SH NAME
cvec_pop \- pop an element from the vector (type-inferred)
.SH LIBRARY
C Collections (libccollections, \-lccollections)
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
#include <ccollections/cvector.h>

value = cvec_pop(v);
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
.nf
Type-inferred wrapper for cvector_pop_back() that gives the popped element
as a value and calls _ccol_fatal_err() when the pop fails.
.fi
.SH PARAMETERS
.nf
v    Vector to pop from
.fi
.SH RETURN VALUE
.nf
The value of the popped element.
.fi
.SH NOTES
.nf
A failure stops the program. The macro gives a value, not a pointer, and
it uses the GNU C statement expression extension.

A vector whose element type is an array, such as char[32], is refused at
compile time, because C can't give back an array as a value. Pop such an
element into a buffer of the element type with cvector_pop_back().
.fi
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cvec_construct(vec, int);
cvec_push(vec, 42);
int val = cvec_pop(vec);  // val == 42
cvec_destroy(vec);
.fi
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR cvector_pop_back (3),
.BR cvec_push (3)
